														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4858043">
									

<p>Absolutely delightful. I love the nonchalantness of the old woman. Like, she puts in a little effort to hide her &quot;trophy husbands&quot; but freely allows the officer to discover them with only the slightest pressure. There's not even any indication that she resists arrest. It almost feels like this behavior is one of those cultural or knowledge &quot;blind spots&quot; people have. Sure she has a vague enough sense that she doesn't want authorities to see her collection, but at the same time she's pretty sure this is what people mean when they talk about a &quot;trophy spouse&quot; and she's been doing it for long enough that the sunk cost fallacy comes into play.</p>
<p>Also the detail that the heads respire, and are alive on (im assuming) a cellular level is intriguing. I imagine they have base reflexes like following things with their eyes, and blinking in sunlight as well. The fact that they respite makes me wonder if they would sneeze if iritated. The even more deep questions arise about their level of mental activity. Is it possible they have something akin to shut-in syndrome? Just a trove of interesting things to consider</p>
<p>unfortunately i can only give it +1, but it is a +1 more than earned</p>

							</div>

								
					
