<p>The narrative of the article is the story of that MTF and their gradual transformation from hopeful, to weary to despairing and begging for rescue. At first they help the foundation in any way they can by communicating with them an informing them of the anomaly and trying to help them document it. Their lack of senses hinder this but they are able to logically deduce where they are and are able to 'sense' the other intangible objects around and in them. After a while they realize they won't be rescued and fall into despair, slowly suffocating as they become tangible enough to need to breath.</p>
<p>As for the communications issue, this is a Foundation long-distance communicator utilizing anomalous tech. As for not being able to see it, at least one of the MTF member down there is able to touch-type from muscle memory.</p>

