									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4874276&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609401592" alt="TheAlienBaby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4874276)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;" >TheAlienBaby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609399507 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">31 Dec 2020 07:25</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13961682/seeking-greenlight:patient-zero">Seeking Greenlight: “Patient Zero”</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4858031">
									

<p>Hey there eNCiVi, I'll be critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am neither an official reviewer (but I am a flight officer) nor a hugely experienced one, so take everything I say with a grain of salt. With that being said, let's begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Section-by-Section&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Elevator Pitch</span></p>
<p>So my main problem with this pitch is in two parts: it is quite overpowered (OP) and it is a humanoid (not a problem in itself, but I'll explain further along).<br />
OP anomalies break the suspension of disbelief of readers if not executed correctly, and said execution is hard to do. Without this execution, OP anomalies feel slightly ridiculous and unrealistic, a surefire way to get downvotes on your article.<br />
Humanoids are one of the hardest types of anomaly to write. Similarly to OP anomalies, they require great execution to not become downvote magnets. Without proper execution, they don't fit with the tone of the Site and feel more like a comic-book character rather than an SCP.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Central Narrative</span></p>
<p>There isn't very much here in regards to narrative. All you have is some testing logs and a vague incident which you fail to elaborate on because it is TBD<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-253107-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-253107-1')">1</a></sup>. This may have been acceptable in Series I, but people expect more in Series VI. Find an emotion you want the readers to feel, and use it to build up your narrative.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:large;">Hook/Attention Grabber</span></p>
<p>This is frustratingly vague and nothing more. Don't keep up the 'mystery' of your concept and try to keep it secret after posting in the forums, explain it! Tell us what the mystery is and what's behind it, otherwise it just makes it harder to critique your idea.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;General&nbsp;Thoughts&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I'm&nbsp;quite&nbsp;doubtful&nbsp;about&nbsp;this</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>To put it bluntly, your anomaly is an OP humanoid which has little to no story behind it besides a vague 'incident' which isn't elaborated on. Not only this, but it is strange to me that it is only immune to the abilities of some of the most dangerous SCPs. Why? I am also getting slight self-insert 'vibes' (for lack of a better word that comes to mind) from this concept, which isn't good. I'd recommend it four things:</p>
<p>1. Consider reworking your concept. As it stands, it's quite OP and contrived.<br />
2. Rework your narrative. Elaborate! Make me feel something!<br />
3. Check out the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/comprehensive-guide-hub">Guide Hub</a> for advice and essays on how to do the above two points. It's a great resource!<br />
4. Contact some reviewers from the <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a>, they have tonnes of experience and are able to provide some great crit!</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Anyway, that's it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-253107-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-253107-1')">1</a>. Always finish off your idea before posting it in the forums, otherwise it makes it more difficult for us critters to critique it.</div>
</div>

